  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **RMSNorm** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, eps=1e-6, weight=None):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    y = x / np.sqrt(np.mean(x*x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n    if weight is not None:\n        y = y * np.asarray(weight, dtype=float)\n    return y.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
